1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,670
Greetings, fellow aliens!

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:05,069
Welcome to the twelfth episode of Earthlings 101.

3
00:00:05,605 --> 00:00:09,228
Today we will learn about the earthlings' most important sense: Vision, or eyesight.

4
00:00:42,141 --> 00:00:46,405
Vision is the capacity to perceive light in order to create a mental image of the environment.

5
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:47,930
But what is light?

6
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:51,438
Light is electromagnetic radiation within a certain range.

7
00:00:51,745 --> 00:01:00,405
The earth atmosphere filters most radiation from the sun, except for three ranges of wavelengths: The radio window, the infrared window, and the optical window.

8
00:01:00,645 --> 00:01:05,085
The latter is between 300 and 1100 nanometers - that's the frequency of light.

9
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:10,824
Earthlings can perceive light between 390 and 700 nanometers - that's called visible light.

10
00:01:11,426 --> 00:01:15,490
The earthlings perceive light with their eyes - a pair of globular organs in the head.

11
00:01:15,872 --> 00:01:24,701
Eyes are primitive biocameras: Light falls through a lens, is focused onto a photosensitive layer called retina, is transformed into electrical signals, and then...

12
00:01:24,701 --> 00:01:27,161
Well, that's when things become interesting.

13
00:01:27,721 --> 00:01:30,970
Earthling sensors are often compared with the sensor system of levy drones.

14
00:01:31,539 --> 00:01:39,579
When the Galactic Tax Authority executes a planetary tax examination, it sends in a Tax Star which releases millions of levy drones to the planet's surface.

15
00:01:40,139 --> 00:01:46,099
Each levy drone is equipped with a multitude of tax assessment sensors, including a sophisticated high-definition camera.

16
00:01:46,679 --> 00:01:55,062
On first glance, a drone camera seems to work exactly like an earthling eye: Light falls through a lens system onto an array of spectroscopic photoreceptors.

17
00:01:55,263 --> 00:02:02,203
The spectroscopic pixel matrix is then sent to the central computer where it is processed and transformed into a 3d voxel model.

18
00:02:02,583 --> 00:02:06,754
Finally, the tax routines compute the monetary value of each taxable entity.

19
00:02:07,078 --> 00:02:12,908
If you take this - minus the tax part - you get a very good explanation of how earthling vision does not work.

20
00:02:12,908 --> 00:02:17,754
Because, from the moment on when the light hits the retina, earthling vision is completely different.

21
00:02:18,116 --> 00:02:25,156
In particular, what the eyes send to the brain is not only pixel data, but also data about contrast, color contrast and motion.

22
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:29,574
In other words, the first step of data processing happens literally within the eyes.

23
00:02:29,917 --> 00:02:34,125
See, the retina consists of light-sensitive cells, rods and cones.

24
00:02:34,125 --> 00:02:40,390
Above those cells we have a thin layer of intermediate neurons, which wire them to the neuro-cables leading to the brain.

25
00:02:40,832 --> 00:02:47,792
Some neurons simply forward information from the rods and cones, but others provide a clever lateral wiring to detect contrast or motion.

26
00:02:48,212 --> 00:02:52,259
For example, one neuron might emit a signal when a certain spot is brighter than its neighbourhood.

27
00:02:53,004 --> 00:02:57,944
In consequence, the cell detects contrast, or, in other words, contours.

28
00:02:57,944 --> 00:03:02,076
Another neuron might only fire when it detects motion in a certain direction.

29
00:03:02,439 --> 00:03:07,999
Still another neuron emits a signal when it perceives a color difference between neighbour spots, and so on.

30
00:03:08,739 --> 00:03:13,474
So, what is sent to the brain is information about motion, contrast and color contrast.

31
00:03:13,817 --> 00:03:15,566
But where is the information sent?

32
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:18,791
The eyes are wired to the Thalamus, in the center of the brain.

33
00:03:19,298 --> 00:03:23,387
"Thalamus" is an ancient word for "inner chamber", and it's kind of a data connection center.

34
00:03:23,753 --> 00:03:27,055
Whoever sends information to the brain must pass through the thalamus.

35
00:03:27,055 --> 00:03:33,838
In particular, the eyes are wired to the two lateral geniculate nuclei - that's just a fancy word for "knee-shaped bumps on the side".

36
00:03:34,099 --> 00:03:39,507
The right bump receives data from the right halves of the retinae of both eyes, the left bump from the left halves.

37
00:03:39,730 --> 00:03:45,630
The information is then forwarded to the visual cortex in the back of the brain where it is processed and sent to the rest of the brain.

38
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:51,536
Spatial and motion data are sent upwards, where they serve to create a dynamic 3D model of the environment.

39
00:03:52,038 --> 00:03:56,058
Color and shape information is sent sidewards and used to identify objects.

40
00:03:58,158 --> 00:03:59,039
Scientific advice.

41
00:03:59,735 --> 00:04:01,962
An interesting field of research is optical illusions.

42
00:04:02,663 --> 00:04:04,123
Take this one, for example.

43
00:04:04,543 --> 00:04:14,323
When you tell an earthling to fix the planet in the center of the image, he will see a green orbiting saucer in the rotating free slot between the pink ones - although there is no green saucer, only pink ones.

44
00:04:14,743 --> 00:04:19,516
The green is an after-image of the pink - maybe due to the color contrast vision I will explain later.

45
00:04:20,039 --> 00:04:23,719
Sometimes the pink saucers will even disappear and he will only see the green one.

46
00:04:25,179 --> 00:04:28,559
Earthlings always center both eyes onto one spot in the visual field.

47
00:04:28,879 --> 00:04:33,079
The centers of the retinae have the highest density of cones and provide the sharpest view.

48
00:04:33,459 --> 00:04:36,430
The farther you are away from the center, the blurrier the vision gets.

49
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:39,410
That's why earthlings always move their eyes around.

50
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:44,450
The brain does a good job in computing the movement away, so the environment appears static.

51
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:49,790
But this doesn't work when you poke the eyeball slightly with a finger - in this case the world seems to move.

52
00:04:51,170 --> 00:04:59,350
As mentioned before, the data received by the visual cortex are used for two purposes: Spatial orientation and motion data, and identifying objects.

53
00:04:59,350 --> 00:05:01,430
Let's start with the former one.

54
00:05:02,230 --> 00:05:11,030
For spatial orientation, having two eyes comes in handy: The brain uses the slight differences between the data from both eyes to estimate the distance of different objects.

55
00:05:11,450 --> 00:05:16,938
Other input data are also taken into account, in particular the smaller angular size of distant objects.

56
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:21,200
The brain uses those data to construct a dynamic 3D model of the environment.

57
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:24,150
Most animals have similar visual systems.

58
00:05:24,667 --> 00:05:31,126
Predators often have frontal eyes with overlapping fields of view, to provide an optimal 3D vision in order to seize their prey.

59
00:05:31,448 --> 00:05:38,228
Prey animals, on the other hand, have often lateral eyes to increase the field of view, so they can detect whoever wants to eat them.

60
00:05:38,548 --> 00:05:40,508
Except for the microbes.

61
00:05:43,928 --> 00:05:46,783
Now to the second point: identifying objects.

62
00:05:47,165 --> 00:05:51,885
This happens in the temporal cortex - that's just a fancy word for "on the sides of the head".

63
00:05:52,525 --> 00:05:55,631
Earthling brains are powerful pattern-recognition machines.

64
00:05:55,631 --> 00:05:59,231
We have already seen that the eyes send contour data to the brain.

65
00:05:59,711 --> 00:06:07,251
What happens is that identified simple contour patterns - corners, edges etc. - are assembled into more and more complex patterns.

66
00:06:07,751 --> 00:06:11,929
Earthlings are great at identifying shapes even from incomplete contour elements.

67
00:06:12,411 --> 00:06:16,311
That's important, for example for identifying partially hidden animals.

68
00:06:16,951 --> 00:06:22,431
When the initial contour elements are not properly aligned, the brain has problems assembling the overall shape.

69
00:06:22,811 --> 00:06:27,451
Those lines, for example, appear as spirals, but they are actually circles.

70
00:06:28,151 --> 00:06:33,011
The pattern recognition of faces is well developed, as it contributes to the recognition of individuals.

71
00:06:33,671 --> 00:06:40,098
Earthling scientists have identified a neuron in a brain that reacts to the celebrity Halle Berry, but not to images of other Earthlings.

72
00:06:40,098 --> 00:06:46,618
The neuron also reacts to Halle Berry in a feline costume covering most of her face, as well as to her name.

73
00:06:47,058 --> 00:06:50,051
So, this cell seems to be a really big fan of Halle Berry.

74
00:06:50,453 --> 00:06:55,633
They also found a neuron that likes Jennifer Aniston, and another one that admires Ronald Reagan.

75
00:06:56,553 --> 00:06:59,229
Recognition of things is mainly based onto shape and color.

76
00:06:59,435 --> 00:07:01,920
The concept of color can be confusing for aliens.

77
00:07:02,506 --> 00:07:06,431
Most educated earthlings would agree that color is a physical property of light.

78
00:07:06,431 --> 00:07:09,231
But as we will see, that is utter nonsense.

79
00:07:09,991 --> 00:07:12,311
Color isn't about physics - it's about biology!

80
00:07:13,431 --> 00:07:17,708
Earthling color perception can be compared to how the Gloobobs of Aldaris 7 perceive sound.

81
00:07:18,377 --> 00:07:21,690
Gloobobs are known for having the worst brass bands in the Galaxy.

82
00:07:22,156 --> 00:07:32,456
It's not their fault: Those creatures have a very primitive audio perception and can only distinguish three ranges of frequencies, called Ged, Bleen, and Droo.

83
00:07:33,856 --> 00:07:39,216
Every sound, every chord or melody they hear will be reduced in their ears to a mix of Ged, Bleen and Droo.

84
00:07:41,556 --> 00:07:45,600
The Gloobob ears contain sound receptors for each one of the three pitch ranges.

85
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:50,564
The sensibilities of the receptors are somewhat fuzzy, so they can tell single sounds apart.

86
00:07:50,564 --> 00:07:53,029
For example, when you play a scale...

87
00:07:56,109 --> 00:07:58,149
Gloobobs hear this.

88
00:08:01,569 --> 00:08:04,149
But they are completely lost when it comes to chords.

89
00:08:05,329 --> 00:08:06,669
Two notes are already too much.

90
00:08:07,669 --> 00:08:16,389
Take for example a chord consisting of Ged and Bleen - for Gloobob ears, that sounds exactly like "Nello", halfway between Ged and Bleen.

91
00:08:17,189 --> 00:08:25,909
So, for Gloobobs, Ged plus Bleen equals Nello, which is of course nonsense - the only thing that is equal is the perception of the sounds by Gloobob ears.

92
00:08:26,609 --> 00:08:34,165
Gloobob scientists have theorized that all sounds belong to a three dimensional "sound space", defined by the perceived intensity of Ged, Bleen and Droo.

93
00:08:34,407 --> 00:08:37,307
Mind, this isn't physics - it's biology.

94
00:08:38,047 --> 00:08:45,155
Gloobob sound recording devices can only produce three sounds - enough to imitate sounds for Gloobob ears, but not for everybody else.

95
00:08:45,495 --> 00:08:49,213
The same holds for Gloobob instruments - hence the bad brass bands.

96
00:08:49,615 --> 00:08:51,104
Why am I telling you this?

97
00:08:51,328 --> 00:08:53,308
Because earthling vision works the same.

98
00:08:53,928 --> 00:08:59,869
Earthlings have only three kinds of color receptors, often called - not quite correctly - red, green and blue.

99
00:08:59,869 --> 00:09:06,111
Even the most complex combination of frequencies are reduced by earthling eyes to a combination of red, green and blue.

100
00:09:06,551 --> 00:09:11,582
For example, earthlings cannot distinguish between monochromatic yellow light and a mix of red and green light.

101
00:09:11,963 --> 00:09:15,802
In both cases, the red and green receptors are excited in the same way.

102
00:09:16,188 --> 00:09:19,254
That's why earthlings say that "red plus green equals yellow".

103
00:09:19,742 --> 00:09:21,519
This is biology, not physics.

104
00:09:22,105 --> 00:09:26,274
In other words, color isn't a physical property - it only exists in the brain.

105
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:32,514
Actually, the expression "red receptor" is misleading - this receptor's peak is rather in the green-yellow range.

106
00:09:32,734 --> 00:09:35,485
This reduces an effect called chromatic aberration.

107
00:09:35,791 --> 00:09:46,107
But anyway, what is sent to the brain is not the raw receptor response but color contrast data - more precisely, yellow-blue contrast, red-green contrast, and luminosity contrast.

108
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:49,547
But what is the advantage of sending color contrast data?

109
00:09:49,927 --> 00:09:53,667
To understand this, we have to understand what color actually is.

110
00:09:53,667 --> 00:10:01,707
When you ask educated adult earthlings what color is, they will probably babble something about frequencies, color circles and additive color blending.

111
00:10:02,029 --> 00:10:07,460
But when you ask earthling cubs, they will talk about blue teddies, yellow flowers and pink sofas.

112
00:10:07,783 --> 00:10:12,468
In other words, they see color not as a property of light, but as a property of objects.

113
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:14,877
And that's actually a much better approach.

114
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:21,300
See, when an earthling has a pink car, it will always be a pink car, no matter how it is lit.

115
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:26,320
Earthling vision relies on whatever light source is available.

116
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:33,540
The reflected light might differ, but for the earthling, his car will always have the same color.

117
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:41,560
So, the word "pink" doesn't actually describe light - it describes how the surface reacts to varying light, as perceived by the earthling eye.

118
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:46,109
So, color is a property of surfaces, which exists only in the brain.

119
00:10:46,332 --> 00:10:47,852
How is this even possible?

120
00:10:48,192 --> 00:10:52,732
Well, what happens is that the brain takes the sensor information and computes the lighting away.

121
00:10:52,732 --> 00:10:57,792
What remains is a perceived property of surfaces, an imaginary material invariant - color.

122
00:10:58,214 --> 00:11:05,754
Here, the color contrast data comes in handy: No matter the lighting, a pink sofa is always pinker than the green carpet it is standing on.

123
00:11:06,754 --> 00:11:10,961
Color is a good example of how earthlings construct a model of reality in their brain.

124
00:11:11,366 --> 00:11:17,199
Physical objects are collections of atoms with properties like shape, size and spectral characteristics of the surface.

125
00:11:17,486 --> 00:11:22,109
But the brain can't directly access to those properties - all it has is sensor information.

126
00:11:22,109 --> 00:11:29,629
So it takes this information, computes factors like lighting and distance away, and constructs simplified models of the objects in the world.

127
00:11:30,009 --> 00:11:34,242
The imaginary properties of the object models correspond more or less to physical reality.

128
00:11:34,726 --> 00:11:41,706
Size and shape are rather accurate approximation of an object's actual geometry, but color is a rough simplification of its spectral characteristics.

129
00:11:42,886 --> 00:11:45,716
So, color is an imaginary property of materials.

130
00:11:46,322 --> 00:11:50,738
This makes sense, as the main purpose of color is actually the identification of materials.

131
00:11:50,738 --> 00:11:55,478
Color allows finding things like flintstone, fertile earth or ripe fruits.

132
00:11:55,918 --> 00:12:03,358
The brain takes out the lighting information to obtain the lighting-invariant "color" and tell different materials apart - even if the reflected light is actually the same.

133
00:12:04,618 --> 00:12:06,591
Colors have a high symbolic meaning.

134
00:12:06,954 --> 00:12:10,465
Blue is perceived as calm and cool, as lakes and oceans are blue.

135
00:12:10,909 --> 00:12:14,087
Green is associated with nature, because plants are green.

136
00:12:14,087 --> 00:12:18,727
Yellow is perceived as joyful and energetic, because earth orbits a yellow star.

137
00:12:19,187 --> 00:12:23,167
Red is associated with violence and danger, as red is the color of fire and blood.

138
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:30,278
Fictional characters are sometimes color-coded for easy identification.

139
00:12:31,255 --> 00:12:36,597
Cartoon characters can often be identified with little more than color information - even humanized animals.

140
00:12:36,597 --> 00:12:41,537
This works also for some live action characters, especially when they wear some sort of uniform.

141
00:12:42,037 --> 00:12:45,213
Colors play also an important part in earthlings' social life.

142
00:12:45,638 --> 00:12:48,801
For example, lovers like to give each other colorful flowers.

143
00:12:49,284 --> 00:12:52,332
There isn't any practical sense, as you can't eat flowers.

144
00:12:52,917 --> 00:12:58,117
There is an old saying amongst alien anthropologists: If it doesn't make sense, it's probably a ritual.

145
00:12:59,477 --> 00:13:00,677
Tips for tourists.

146
00:13:01,377 --> 00:13:08,157
If you want to watch an earthling movie, don't expect realistic colors: Earthling cameras can only record three color components.

147
00:13:08,897 --> 00:13:12,156
Personally, I find black-and-white movies less disturbing.

148
00:13:12,763 --> 00:13:17,563
Above all, stay away from so-called 3D movies, especially if you have only one eye.

149
00:13:18,503 --> 00:13:22,586
It shall be noted that some female earthlings have four types of cones instead of three.

150
00:13:22,926 --> 00:13:26,358
In earthling terms, they have a four-dimensional color space.

151
00:13:26,358 --> 00:13:30,530
There are also accounts on individuals able to perceive an additional color called octarine.

152
00:13:31,154 --> 00:13:39,100
But the same accounts also report an unregistered habitable planar super-structure with bio-propulsion, as well as other oddities, so this is probably fiction.

153
00:13:39,522 --> 00:13:45,462
Anyway, this is nothing compared with an aquatic animal called the mantis shrimp which has a sixteen-dimensional color space.

154
00:13:47,442 --> 00:13:48,450
Strategic advice.

155
00:13:48,891 --> 00:14:04,351
Mantis shrimps would make a good base to breed super-soldiers: Their color vision would make earthling camouflage useless, they have sharp appendages they can accelerate to the speed of earthlings weapons projectiles, they wear a natural body armour, and they can move so fast that the liquid around them starts boiling.

156
00:14:04,811 --> 00:14:07,364
However, you might want to do something about their size.

157
00:14:07,566 --> 00:14:15,006
I will conclude with an open question: Spectral violet, the light at the upper end of the visual spectrum, is allegedly perceived as slightly reddish.

158
00:14:15,408 --> 00:14:19,350
That's why earthlings bend the spectrum to a circle - the color wheel.

159
00:14:19,350 --> 00:14:24,150
But violet light is far off the so-called red receptors - why is it perceived as reddish?

160
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:25,984
I see two possibilities.

161
00:14:26,429 --> 00:14:29,350
Either the red receptors have a second bump in the violet zone.

162
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:35,894
Or spectral violet isn't actually perceived as reddish blue, but as deep blue, and the name "violet" is actually a misnomer.

163
00:14:36,095 --> 00:14:40,401
The fact that computer screens can't display spectral violet might add to the confusion.

164
00:14:40,401 --> 00:14:42,301
I honestly don't know.

165
00:14:42,541 --> 00:14:45,648
So I'll ask my earthling viewers: What do you think?

166
00:14:45,975 --> 00:14:53,966
And if you have, say, access to a violet laser, or a violet light weapon: Does spectral violet actually appear reddish, or rather deep blue?

167
00:14:54,167 --> 00:14:56,147
If it's reddish: How comes?

168
00:14:56,387 --> 00:14:58,996
If it's deep blue: Why the color wheel?

169
00:14:58,996 --> 00:15:02,171
This was the twelfth episode of Earthlings 101.

170
00:15:02,659 --> 00:15:08,969
Next time we will speak about earthling mathematics - a science of truth, space, numbers, and the gender of Blobblings.

171
00:15:09,937 --> 00:15:15,027
Thanks for watching, click on "like" if you liked it, and as always: Don't forget to be alien!

